          "text": "This week, Jeremi and Zachary are joined by Dr. Marc-William Palen to discuss the history of free trade and associated hopes for international peace.\n\nZachary sets the scene with his poem entitled, “A World at Sail”\n\nMarc-William Palen is a historian at the University of Exeter. His new book, "
        },
        {
          "text": "Pax Economica: Left-Wing Visions of a Free Trade World",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " (Princeton University Press), was published in early 2024 and has been named among the year’s “best books” by the "
        },
        {
          "text": "New Yorker",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". His other publications include "
        },
        {
          "text": "The ‘”Conspiracy” of Free Trade: The Anglo-American Struggle over Empire and Economic Globalisation, 1846-1896",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " (Cambridge University Press, 2016). His work has also appeared in "
        },
